{"text": "As you walk towards the figure, ask who teaches this. Becky traces a wave of books in the 1970s on the correct way to wear kimono. One large school opened in 1964 and, Beck notes, runs five academies in Japan's biggest cities. The first layer goes on. In one Japanese case study, a professional dressing of a furisode used 16 separate items: padding, underlayers, cords, boards, an obi pillow. Together they weighed about three kilograms, nearly four times a sweater and jeans. Left over right is old. Becky traces it to a clothing code of the year 718, which followed Chinese fashion. The fold at the waist is easily disturbed. In the yukata study, a bow made kneeling on the floor shifted it most, a standing bow least. Women today tie the obi high from under the bust to the waist. About a century ago, cords and obi sat low at the hip bones. The knot is tied last at the back. Walk round and look.", "duration": 67.7, "timestamps": {"word": [{"word": "As", "start": 0.12, "end": 0.28}, {"word": "you", "start": 0.34, "end": 0.44}, {"word": "walk", "start": 0.56, "end": 0.78}, {"word": "towards", "start": 0.84, "end": 1.22}, {"word": "the", "start": 1.28, "end": 1.34}, {"word": "figure,", "start": 1.4, "end": 1.66}, {"word": "ask", "start": 2.12, "end": 2.36}, {"word": "who", "start": 2.4, "end": 2.56}, {"word": "teaches", "start": 2.62, "end": 3.04}, {"word": "this.", "start": 3.12, "end": 3.44}, {"word": "Becky", "start": 4.14, "end": 4.44}, {"word": "traces", "start": 4.5, "end": 4.86}, {"word": "a", "start": 4.92, "end": 4.96}, {"word": "wave", "start": 5.1, "end": 5.38}, {"word": "of", "start": 5.42, "end": 5.54}, {"word": "books", "start": 5.6, "end": 5.86}, {"word": "in", "start": 5.9, "end": 5.98}, {"word": "the", "start": 6, "end": 6.06}, {"word": "1970s", "start": 6.12, "end": 7.14}, {"word": "on", "start": 7.28, "end": 7.36}, {"word": "the", "start": 7.38, "end": 7.46}, {"word": "correct", "start": 7.52, "end": 7.88}, {"word": "way", "start": 7.94, "end": 8.